<workout_file>
	<author>Jarvis Chau (via TrainingPeaks)</author>
	<name>Over/Under Tens</name>
	<description>One of TrainingPeaks Virtual&apos;s classic workouts:
Over/Under Tens.

A quick warm-up, followed by 2x 10 minute efforts during which we&apos;ll switch between over and under your FTP, to help train your body to recover at high intensity. Simple, but effective.</description>
	<sportType>bike</sportType>
	<tags/>
	<workout>
		<Warmup Duration="240" PowerHigh="0.7" PowerLow="0.5" Cadence="90">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
10:Welcome to Over/Under Tens;
20:This classic workout is perfect for improving your ability to recover after a sprint in the middle of a race.;
30:We&amp;apos;ll do two blocks of 10 minutes just above your FTP, with minimal rest inbetween.;
60:For now, focus on warming up, and getting your legs spinning.;
120:Half way through the warmup.;
180:1 minute to go.;
}"/>
		</Warmup>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="1.07">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Bring the power up to just over your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
90:30 seconds to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="180" Power="0.97">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Ease the power down slightly, but we&apos;re still working hard.;
30:Settle in and focus on smooth pedalling.;
60:Feel your body starting to recover.;
120:1 minute to go, and then we&apos;re going back up again.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="1.07">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Bring the power up to just over your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
90:30 seconds to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="180" Power="0.97">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Ease the power down slightly, but we&apos;re still working hard.;
30:Settle in and focus on smooth pedalling.;
60:Feel your body starting to recover.;
120:1 minute to go, and then we&apos;ll have a short break.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.55">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:...and relax.;
30:Take on some fluids and take your time to recover.;
60:There&apos;s just 1 minute left until the next effort.;
90:30 seconds to go.;
110:10 seconds to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="1.07">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Bring the power up to just over your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
90:30 seconds to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="180" Power="0.97">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Ease the power down slightly, but we&apos;re still working hard.;
30:Settle in and focus on smooth pedalling.;
60:Feel your body starting to recover.;
120:1 minute to go, and then we&apos;re going back up again.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="1.07">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Bring the power up to just over your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
90:30 seconds to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="180" Power="0.97">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Ease the power down slightly, but we&apos;re still working hard.;
30:Settle in and focus on smooth pedalling.;
60:Feel your body starting to recover.;
120:1 minute to go, and then we&apos;re done.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<Cooldown Duration="240" PowerHigh="0.55" PowerLow="0.75">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:...and relax.;
30:Take on some fluids and start to wind it down.;
60:There&amp;apos;s 3 minutes left until the end.;
70:The power will ramp down slowly while you recover.;
180:Great job today.;
190:Looking forward to working out with you again soon.;
}"/>
		</Cooldown>
	</workout>
</workout_file>